WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:05.469
P1.1 · P&L year to date, cumulative balance sheet

2
00:00:06.619 --> 00:00:10.669
The P&L restarts at zero at the start of each fiscal year.

3
00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:14.170
The balance sheet is cumulative: balances at a date.

4
00:00:16.619 --> 00:00:22.830
Here is the P&L, month by month, built from the ledger lines and each account's classification.

5
00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:27.452
Each version is a closing: pick one month, or all of them side by side.

6
00:00:28.602 --> 00:00:31.589
The balance sheet shows balances at each month end.

7
00:00:31.639 --> 00:00:37.922
In a group view, intercompany balances are eliminated, so the total intercompany line is zero.

8
00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:45.335
The cash flow statement is derived from both: net income, then the changes in working capital.

9
00:00:45.385 --> 00:00:47.934
Each month is compared with the month before.

10
00:00:49.084 --> 00:00:52.612
If either fails, look at account classification first.

11
00:00:57.384 --> 00:01:01.118
Next: P1.2  Drilling down to ledger lines

